Z||000000||jhar1987||07-03-2000||07:33 PM||||need help, came across a super 3800 with 28k, for $900.00 need to move quickly. can anyone tell me what is needed to complete the coversion? and what all is needed from the donor car? thanks jeff  85 v6||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||07-03-2000||08:13 PM||||What year engine is it and what trans will you use?<P>Get the engine, the complete engine harness, ECM, plastic fuel lines as far down as you can, air filter box, vats module/key (or passkey box), exhaust pipe down to the cat, A/C compressor and lines, fuse/relay box, and the trans if you can afford it.<P>Anything else you folks can think of?<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||07-03-2000||08:19 PM||||Bear in mind, I've never done a 3800 swap, but I've thought about it and read some about it. Common sense tells us that you need to get the entire complete engine, motor mounts, ECM, and the wiring harness from the donor car. The tranny is what I'm not sure about. Lots of people swap in the 4 speed auto OD out of the donor car too. Hopefully, other Forum members, or maybe even Phil, will fill us in on anything I left out Good luck.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 07-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||07-03-2000||08:56 PM||||The 3800SC's came with 4T60EHD's (92-96) or 4T65E's (97-2000). <P>You either go with the 4T6xE trans or get a custom made flywheel and fake out the ECM.<P>While I've only swapped a SC engine into an A car (I'm in the middle of the 3.4L DOHC swap), the A car mounts should work with little effort.<P>Frankly, figure another $500 to $1000 to make it run. Exhaust, mounts, custom dogbone and 100 hours of work. The oil filter adapter will need changing depending on the year of the engine. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||07-03-2000||11:27 PM||||man jump on that I payed more than that for a 50k mile non-supercharged engine!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Guinea Pig||07-04-2000||02:51 AM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com," TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com,</A>  he has a very informative site on 3800 conversions.<BR>Then go to <A HREF="http://www.twinlakesfiero.tripod.com." TARGET=_blank>www.twinlakesfiero.tripod.com.</A> <BR>Bob is putting a supercharged 3800 in my car.<BR>He can give you a knowledgeable perspective on what it takes to install these engines.  I've stayed with the automatic from the donor for my car.  The most difficult and time consuming part of the conversion appears to be the harness.  ||||reg||1
